	(text "PA-DRAIN SAFETY INTERLOCK (H2-C, INTERLOCK_SPEC + AMENDMENTS A1/A3/A6)\nThresholds (ratiometric to +1V8_DIG / IL_REF, 0.1% resistors):\n- Gate lost: IL_REF_LOST 1.009 V -> PA gate > -0.15 V (worst -0.19..-0.11 V) pulls GATES_OK low\n- Gate pinched: IL_REF_PINCH 0.737 V -> gate < -1.50 V (worst -1.58..-1.42 V) releases GATES_PINCHED\n- -5V_BF trip -4.60 V (worst -4.78..-4.42 V); -3V3_SW trip -3.00 V (worst -3.13..-2.87 V)\n- +3V3_AUX UV (U908 ch C): trips below ~2.97 V\nNEG_OK = NEG_RAILS_OK AND GATES_OK (U912). IL_CLR_N = MCU_PA_EN AND WDT_OK AND NEG_OK (U911).\nPA_ARMED = U909 Q, clocked by MCU_PA_EN delayed 5.5-9.9 us (R964/C912 + U910 Schmitt), D = GATES_PINCHED.\nPA_DRAIN_EN = PA_ARMED AND WDT_OK AND NEG_OK (U705 on MCU sheet), R965 100k pull-down."
	(at 25.4 330.2 0)
	(effects
		(font
			(size 1.27 1.27)
		)
	)
	(uuid "4ffef7af-6e68-4735-b237-53690b0eb664")
)
	(text "FAIL-SAFE BEHAVIOUR\n- Open-collector nets NEG_RAILS_OK, GATES_OK, GATES_PINCHED: 10k to +3V3_AUX / 10k to GND (high 1.57-1.73 V).\n  +3V3_AUX absent -> comparators unpowered, nets pulled to 0 V -> NEG_OK low -> drain off.\n- IL_REF (gate-divider + gate-reference supply) = +1V8_DIG via U914 TPS22917, ON = NEG_RAILS_OK.\n  Neg rails not OK -> IL_REF off and discharged (QOD via R972 100R): no positive bias into unpowered PA gates.\n  Gate-comparator inputs may then sit below GND (<=~0.1 mA via 49.9k, LM339B abs max -50 mA); their outputs are\n  undefined (SNOAA35 6.9.2) but NEG_OK is already forced low by NEG_RAILS_OK through U912.\n- Any fault latches PA_ARMED low via IL_CLR_N; re-arm only by MCU_PA_EN low->high with gates pinched.\n- +1V8_DIG absent -> logic unpowered (Ioff), R965 holds PA_DRAIN_EN low.\n- U908 ch D spare: TI SNOAA35 9.1.2 'VOL Full VID' (IN- 10k to V+, IN+ 10k to GND), output left open (9.1.3).\nDatasheets: LM339B SLCS006Z, SNOAA35F; TPS22917 SLVSDW8B; SN74LVC1G74 SCES794G; LVC1G17 SCES351Y; LVC1G11 SCES487I."
	(at 25.4 383.54 0)
	(effects
		(font
			(size 1.27 1.27)
		)
	)
	(uuid "85e357e0-eabc-4e05-a90f-13be47d7c580")
)
	(text "H2-C sim fix: IL_EN = NEG_RAILS_OK AND PG_3V3RF (U915, 100k pull-down R973) drives TPS22917 ON and U912 input A, so NEG_OK = NEG_RAILS_OK . PG_3V3RF . GATES_OK. Reason: behavioural sim showed LM339 outputs float below 2 V supply during +3V3_AUX ramp -> NEG_RAILS_OK mid-level could switch IL_REF on while ADAR1000 unpowered (+0.63 V on VGG_PA). PG_3V3RF (TPS568230 PGOOD, low during soft-start / FB<85%) is low until AVDD3 is regulated."
	(at 400 295 0)
	(effects
		(font
			(size 1.27 1.27)
		)
	)
	(uuid "e15cac37-06d2-4c2f-ba82-7e8bbd1c89ea")
)
	(text "REC hardware (H2C_SEQUENCING_SIM.md rev 2, items 5-9; parts: REC_PARTS.md / IMPL_REC.md):\n- U920 TPS386000 (SBVS105F): SENSE1 +1V8_DIG 1.671 V (R977 32.4k / R978 10.2k), SENSE2 +3V3_AUX 2.968 V (R979 64.2k / R1000 10.0k);\n  RESET1/RESET2 open-drain wired-AND onto PG_3V3RF; tD = 9.6 ms (CT1/CT2 2.2 nF, Eq 8); outputs valid for VDD >= 0.9 V.\n  VDD = IL_SUP_VDD = BAT54C D960 diode-OR of +3V3_RF / +5V_PA, C935 100 nF. MR = VDD, WDI = GND, SENSE3/4L/4H = GND,\n  unused open-drain RESET3/RESET4/WDO joined on IL_SUP_OD with R1001 1M pull-up; CT3, CT4 open (fixed delay, p4), VREF open (IDD test cond.).\n- Active-high 2nd output realised as inverter Q966 (gate PG_3V3RF, R976 100k to IL_SUP_VDD) -> IL_Q3G -> Q965 (Q3)\n  clamps TPS22917 ON (IL_ON); R974 10k from IL_EN to IL_ON. U912 A stays on IL_EN.\n- D961 BAT54C: cathode PG_3V3RF, anodes PA_DRAIN_EN and IL_CLR_N; 1k series R735 (U705 Y, mcu sheet) and R975 (U911 Y).\n- U921 TLV75518P: IN +3V3_RF (C938 1 uF), EN = PG_3V3RF, OUT IL_REF_SRC (C914 1 uF) -> U914 VIN (was +1V8_DIG).\n- C915 IL_REF decoupling 100 nF -> 10 nF.\n- U908 ch D: +3V3_RF UV 3.10 V: R971 49.9k / R970 10.2k (IL_RFMON) on pin 11, pin 10 = IL_REF_N5V, pin 13 -> NEG_RAILS_OK.\n- Crowbars (items 1-4) are on the POWER_SEQUENCING sheet next to U621-U624.\nOPEN: supervisor sink current with clamps ~2.4 mA > 1 mA VOL spec; TLV755 EN VLO 0.3 V not guaranteed (see IMPL_REC.md)."
	(at 330.2 450.85 0)
	(effects
		(font
			(size 1.27 1.27)
		)
	)
	(uuid "d666bd7c-12b4-429a-9aa3-9c87d7d4138b")
